{"parents": [{"link": "../../", "title": "API Reference"}, {"link": "../", "title": "auth0_api_python"}], "prev": {"link": "../types/", "title": "auth0_api_python.types"}, "next": null, "title": "auth0_api_python.utils", "meta": {}, "body": "<section id=\"module-auth0_api_python.utils\">\n<span id=\"auth0-api-python-utils\"></span><h1>auth0_api_python.utils<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#module-auth0_api_python.utils\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h1>\n<p>Utility functions for OIDC discovery and JWKS fetching (asynchronously)\nusing httpx or a custom fetch approach.</p>\n<section id=\"functions\">\n<h2>Functions<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#functions\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2>\n<table class=\"autosummary longtable docutils align-default\">\n<tbody>\n<tr class=\"row-odd\"><td><p><a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#auth0_api_python.utils.parse_cache_control_max_age\" title=\"auth0_api_python.utils.parse_cache_control_max_age\"><code class=\"xref py py-obj docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">parse_cache_control_max_age</span></code></a>(\u2192\u00a0Optional[int])</p></td>\n<td><p>Parse the max-age directive from a Cache-Control HTTP header.</p></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"row-even\"><td><p><a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#auth0_api_python.utils.normalize_domain\" title=\"auth0_api_python.utils.normalize_domain\"><code class=\"xref py py-obj docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">normalize_domain</span></code></a>(\u2192\u00a0str)</p></td>\n<td><p>Normalize a domain string to a standard issuer URL format.</p></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"row-odd\"><td><p><a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#auth0_api_python.utils.is_auth_server_outage\" title=\"auth0_api_python.utils.is_auth_server_outage\"><code class=\"xref py py-obj docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">is_auth_server_outage</span></code></a>(\u2192\u00a0bool)</p></td>\n<td><p>Check whether a discovery or JWKS fetch error means the auth server is down or overloaded.</p></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"row-even\"><td><p><a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#auth0_api_python.utils.fetch_oidc_metadata\" title=\"auth0_api_python.utils.fetch_oidc_metadata\"><code class=\"xref py py-obj docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">fetch_oidc_metadata</span></code></a>(\u2192\u00a0tuple[dict[str,\u00a0Any],\u00a0Optional[int]])</p></td>\n<td><p>Asynchronously fetch the OIDC config from <a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https:/\">https:/</a>/{domain}/.well-known/openid-configuration.</p></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"row-odd\"><td><p><a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#auth0_api_python.utils.fetch_jwks\" title=\"auth0_api_python.utils.fetch_jwks\"><code class=\"xref py py-obj docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">fetch_jwks</span></code></a>(\u2192\u00a0tuple[dict[str,\u00a0Any],\u00a0Optional[int]])</p></td>\n<td><p>Asynchronously fetch the JSON Web Key Set from jwks_uri.</p></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"row-even\"><td><p><a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#auth0_api_python.utils.get_unverified_header\" title=\"auth0_api_python.utils.get_unverified_header\"><code class=\"xref py py-obj docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">get_unverified_header</span></code></a>(\u2192\u00a0dict)</p></td>\n<td><p>Parse the JWT header without verifying signature.</p></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"row-odd\"><td><p><a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#auth0_api_python.utils.get_unverified_payload\" title=\"auth0_api_python.utils.get_unverified_payload\"><code class=\"xref py py-obj docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">get_unverified_payload</span></code></a>(\u2192\u00a0dict)</p></td>\n<td><p>Parse the JWT payload without verifying signature.</p></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"row-even\"><td><p><a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#auth0_api_python.utils.fix_base64_padding\" title=\"auth0_api_python.utils.fix_base64_padding\"><code class=\"xref py py-obj docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">fix_base64_padding</span></code></a>(\u2192\u00a0str)</p></td>\n<td><p>If <cite>segment</cite>'s length is not a multiple of 4, add '=' padding</p></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"row-odd\"><td><p><a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#auth0_api_python.utils.remove_bytes_prefix\" title=\"auth0_api_python.utils.remove_bytes_prefix\"><code class=\"xref py py-obj docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">remove_bytes_prefix</span></code></a>(\u2192\u00a0str)</p></td>\n<td><p>If the string looks like b'eyJh...', remove the leading b' and trailing '.</p></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"row-even\"><td><p><a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#auth0_api_python.utils.normalize_url_for_htu\" title=\"auth0_api_python.utils.normalize_url_for_htu\"><code class=\"xref py py-obj docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">normalize_url_for_htu</span></code></a>(\u2192\u00a0str)</p></td>\n<td><p>Normalize URL for DPoP htu comparison .</p></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"row-odd\"><td><p><a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#auth0_api_python.utils.sha256_base64url\" title=\"auth0_api_python.utils.sha256_base64url\"><code class=\"xref py py-obj docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">sha256_base64url</span></code></a>(\u2192\u00a0str)</p></td>\n<td><p>Compute SHA-256 digest of the input string and return a</p></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"row-even\"><td><p><a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#auth0_api_python.utils.calculate_jwk_thumbprint\" title=\"auth0_api_python.utils.calculate_jwk_thumbprint\"><code class=\"xref py py-obj docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">calculate_jwk_thumbprint</span></code></a>(\u2192\u00a0str)</p></td>\n<td><p>Compute the RFC 7638 JWK thumbprint for a public JWK.</p></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n</section>\n<section id=\"module-contents\">\n<h2>Module Contents<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#module-contents\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2>\n<dl class=\"py function\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"auth0_api_python.utils.parse_cache_control_max_age\">\n<span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">auth0_api_python.utils.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">parse_cache_control_max_age</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">headers</span></span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">collections.abc.Mapping</span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">[</span></span><span class=\"pre\">str</span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">,</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"pre\">str</span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">]</span></span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span> <span class=\"sig-return\"><span class=\"sig-return-icon\">&#x2192;</span> <span class=\"sig-return-typehint\"><span class=\"pre\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">|</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#auth0_api_python.utils.parse_cache_control_max_age\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Parse the max-age directive from a Cache-Control HTTP header.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p><strong>headers</strong> \u2013 HTTP response headers (dict-like, supports case-insensitive\naccess for httpx Headers objects)</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Returns<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p>max-age value in seconds, or None if not present or unparseable</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py function\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"auth0_api_python.utils.normalize_domain\">\n<span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">auth0_api_python.utils.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">normalize_domain</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">domain</span></span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">str</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span> <span class=\"sig-return\"><span class=\"sig-return-icon\">&#x2192;</span> <span class=\"sig-return-typehint\"><span class=\"pre\">str</span></span></span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#auth0_api_python.utils.normalize_domain\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Normalize a domain string to a standard issuer URL format.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p><strong>domain</strong> \u2013 Domain string in any format (e.g., \u201ctenant.auth0.com\u201d,\n\u201c<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://tenant.auth0.com/\">https://tenant.auth0.com/</a>\u201d, \u201cTENANT.AUTH0.COM\u201d)</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Returns<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p>//tenant.auth0.com/\u201d)</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p>Normalized issuer URL (e.g., \u201chttps</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py function\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"auth0_api_python.utils.is_auth_server_outage\">\n<span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">auth0_api_python.utils.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">is_auth_server_outage</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">error</span></span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">Exception</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span> <span class=\"sig-return\"><span class=\"sig-return-icon\">&#x2192;</span> <span class=\"sig-return-typehint\"><span class=\"pre\">bool</span></span></span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#auth0_api_python.utils.is_auth_server_outage\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Check whether a discovery or JWKS fetch error means the auth server is down or overloaded.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p><strong>error</strong> \u2013 The exception raised while fetching.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Returns<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p>True for connection errors, timeouts, HTTP 5xx and HTTP 429. False for anything else.</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py function\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"auth0_api_python.utils.fetch_oidc_metadata\">\n<em class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">async</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></em><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">auth0_api_python.utils.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">fetch_oidc_metadata</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">domain</span></span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">str</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">custom_fetch</span></span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">Callable</span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">[</span></span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">...</span></span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">,</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"pre\">Any</span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">]</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">|</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span> <span class=\"sig-return\"><span class=\"sig-return-icon\">&#x2192;</span> <span class=\"sig-return-typehint\"><span class=\"pre\">tuple</span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">[</span></span><span class=\"pre\">dict</span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">[</span></span><span class=\"pre\">str</span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">,</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"pre\">Any</span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">]</span></span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">,</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"pre\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">|</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"pre\">None</span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">]</span></span></span></span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#auth0_api_python.utils.fetch_oidc_metadata\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Asynchronously fetch the OIDC config from <a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https:/\">https:/</a>/{domain}/.well-known/openid-configuration.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Returns<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p>Tuple of (metadata_dict, max_age_or_none). max_age is parsed from\nthe Cache-Control response header if present.</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py function\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"auth0_api_python.utils.fetch_jwks\">\n<em class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">async</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></em><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">auth0_api_python.utils.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">fetch_jwks</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">jwks_uri</span></span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">str</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">custom_fetch</span></span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">Callable</span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">[</span></span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">...</span></span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">,</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"pre\">Any</span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">]</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">|</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span> <span class=\"sig-return\"><span class=\"sig-return-icon\">&#x2192;</span> <span class=\"sig-return-typehint\"><span class=\"pre\">tuple</span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">[</span></span><span class=\"pre\">dict</span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">[</span></span><span class=\"pre\">str</span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">,</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"pre\">Any</span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">]</span></span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">,</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"pre\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">|</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"pre\">None</span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">]</span></span></span></span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#auth0_api_python.utils.fetch_jwks\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Asynchronously fetch the JSON Web Key Set from jwks_uri.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Returns<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p>Tuple of (jwks_dict, max_age_or_none). max_age is parsed from\nthe Cache-Control response header if present.</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py function\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"auth0_api_python.utils.get_unverified_header\">\n<span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">auth0_api_python.utils.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">get_unverified_header</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">token</span></span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">str</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">|</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"pre\">bytes</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span> <span class=\"sig-return\"><span class=\"sig-return-icon\">&#x2192;</span> <span class=\"sig-return-typehint\"><span class=\"pre\">dict</span></span></span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#auth0_api_python.utils.get_unverified_header\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Parse the JWT header without verifying signature.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p><strong>token</strong> \u2013 The JWT token</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Returns<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p>Decoded header as dictionary</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py function\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"auth0_api_python.utils.get_unverified_payload\">\n<span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">auth0_api_python.utils.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">get_unverified_payload</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">token</span></span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">str</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">|</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"pre\">bytes</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span> <span class=\"sig-return\"><span class=\"sig-return-icon\">&#x2192;</span> <span class=\"sig-return-typehint\"><span class=\"pre\">dict</span></span></span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#auth0_api_python.utils.get_unverified_payload\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Parse the JWT payload without verifying signature.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p><strong>token</strong> \u2013 The JWT token</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Returns<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p>Decoded payload (claims) as dictionary</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py function\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"auth0_api_python.utils.fix_base64_padding\">\n<span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">auth0_api_python.utils.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">fix_base64_padding</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">segment</span></span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">str</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span> <span class=\"sig-return\"><span class=\"sig-return-icon\">&#x2192;</span> <span class=\"sig-return-typehint\"><span class=\"pre\">str</span></span></span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#auth0_api_python.utils.fix_base64_padding\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>If <cite>segment</cite>\u2019s length is not a multiple of 4, add \u2018=\u2019 padding\nso that base64.urlsafe_b64decode won\u2019t produce nonsense bytes.\nNo extra \u2018=\u2019 added if length is already a multiple of 4.</p>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py function\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"auth0_api_python.utils.remove_bytes_prefix\">\n<span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">auth0_api_python.utils.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">remove_bytes_prefix</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">s</span></span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">str</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span> <span class=\"sig-return\"><span class=\"sig-return-icon\">&#x2192;</span> <span class=\"sig-return-typehint\"><span class=\"pre\">str</span></span></span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#auth0_api_python.utils.remove_bytes_prefix\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>If the string looks like b\u2019eyJh\u2026\u2019, remove the leading b\u2019 and trailing \u2018.</p>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py function\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"auth0_api_python.utils.normalize_url_for_htu\">\n<span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">auth0_api_python.utils.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">normalize_url_for_htu</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">raw_url</span></span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">str</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span> <span class=\"sig-return\"><span class=\"sig-return-icon\">&#x2192;</span> <span class=\"sig-return-typehint\"><span class=\"pre\">str</span></span></span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#auth0_api_python.utils.normalize_url_for_htu\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Normalize URL for DPoP htu comparison .</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p><strong>raw_url</strong> \u2013 The raw URL string to normalize</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Returns<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p>The normalized URL string</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Raises<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p><strong>ValueError</strong> \u2013 If the URL is invalid or cannot be parsed</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py function\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"auth0_api_python.utils.sha256_base64url\">\n<span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">auth0_api_python.utils.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">sha256_base64url</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">input_str</span></span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">str</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">|</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"pre\">bytes</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span> <span class=\"sig-return\"><span class=\"sig-return-icon\">&#x2192;</span> <span class=\"sig-return-typehint\"><span class=\"pre\">str</span></span></span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#auth0_api_python.utils.sha256_base64url\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Compute SHA-256 digest of the input string and return a\nBase64URL-encoded string <em>without</em> padding.</p>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py function\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"auth0_api_python.utils.calculate_jwk_thumbprint\">\n<span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">auth0_api_python.utils.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">calculate_jwk_thumbprint</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">jwk</span></span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">dict</span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">[</span></span><span class=\"pre\">str</span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">,</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"pre\">str</span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">]</span></span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span> <span class=\"sig-return\"><span class=\"sig-return-icon\">&#x2192;</span> <span class=\"sig-return-typehint\"><span class=\"pre\">str</span></span></span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#auth0_api_python.utils.calculate_jwk_thumbprint\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Compute the RFC 7638 JWK thumbprint for a public JWK.</p>\n<ul class=\"simple\">\n<li><p>For EC keys, includes only: crv, kty, x, y</p></li>\n<li><p>Serializes with no whitespace, keys sorted lexicographically</p></li>\n<li><p>Hashes with SHA-256 and returns base64url-encoded string without padding</p></li>\n</ul>\n</dd></dl>\n\n</section>\n</section>\n", "metatags": "<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\" />\n", "rellinks": [["genindex", "General Index", "I", "index"], ["py-modindex", "Python Module Index", "", "modules"], ["autoapi/auth0_api_python/types/index", "auth0_api_python.types", "P", "previous"]], "sourcename": "autoapi/auth0_api_python/utils/index.rst.txt", "toc": "<ul>\n<li><a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#\">auth0_api_python.utils</a><ul>\n<li><a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#functions\">Functions</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#module-contents\">Module Contents</a><ul>\n<li><a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#auth0_api_python.utils.parse_cache_control_max_age\"><code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">parse_cache_control_max_age()</span></code></a></li>\n<li><a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#auth0_api_python.utils.normalize_domain\"><code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">normalize_domain()</span></code></a></li>\n<li><a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#auth0_api_python.utils.is_auth_server_outage\"><code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">is_auth_server_outage()</span></code></a></li>\n<li><a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#auth0_api_python.utils.fetch_oidc_metadata\"><code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">fetch_oidc_metadata()</span></code></a></li>\n<li><a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#auth0_api_python.utils.fetch_jwks\"><code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">fetch_jwks()</span></code></a></li>\n<li><a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#auth0_api_python.utils.get_unverified_header\"><code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">get_unverified_header()</span></code></a></li>\n<li><a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#auth0_api_python.utils.get_unverified_payload\"><code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">get_unverified_payload()</span></code></a></li>\n<li><a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#auth0_api_python.utils.fix_base64_padding\"><code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">fix_base64_padding()</span></code></a></li>\n<li><a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#auth0_api_python.utils.remove_bytes_prefix\"><code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">remove_bytes_prefix()</span></code></a></li>\n<li><a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#auth0_api_python.utils.normalize_url_for_htu\"><code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">normalize_url_for_htu()</span></code></a></li>\n<li><a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#auth0_api_python.utils.sha256_base64url\"><code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">sha256_base64url()</span></code></a></li>\n<li><a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#auth0_api_python.utils.calculate_jwk_thumbprint\"><code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">calculate_jwk_thumbprint()</span></code></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n", "display_toc": true, "page_source_suffix": ".rst", "current_page_name": "autoapi/auth0_api_python/utils/index", "sidebars": ["about.html", "searchfield.html", "navigation.html", "relations.html", "donate.html"], "alabaster_version": "1.0.0", "alabaster_version_info": [1, 0, 0]}